    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2564" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶνος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰν&lt;&gt;<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έω</span></span>) poet. and 
			Ion.
		 word, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tale,
			story</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.652
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.508
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				534
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰνεῖν αἶνον</span> to
			tell <i>a tale</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1483
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1380
			</span></i>: esp. <i>story with moral, fable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				202
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				86
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				89
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκουε δὴ τὸν αἶνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Iamb.</u>
					1.211
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>saying, proverb</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλαιὸς αἶ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					508
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				14.43
			</span></i>; <i>riddle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Carm.Pop.
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			=
			
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπαινος</span>, <i>praise</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.795
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.110
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτύμβιος αἶ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1547
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				780
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				707
			</span></i> (all lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξιος αἴνου μεγάλου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.107
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαίνου</span>
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ps.</u>
				8.2
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				18.43
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>decree, resolution</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν Ἀχαιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					4.926
				</span></i>
			 (Epid.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ αἶνον</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ψήφισμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				672.15
			</span></i> (Delph.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				36.16
			</span></i>.</div>
